# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REC Code — where configuration lives
#
# There is no root .env: each process reads its own file in development and
# its service manager's environment in production. Never commit real
# secrets; .env and .env.* are gitignored except *.env.example.
#
#   apps/web/.env.local           ← apps/web/.env.example
#                                   web app + seed. The scheduler falls back
#                                   to this file in development.
#   apps/judge-worker/.env.local  ← apps/judge-worker/.env.example
#                                   judge worker (no database credentials).
#   apps/scheduler/.env.local     optional scheduler-only overrides.
#   packages/db/.env              ← the two lines below
#                                   Prisma CLI (pnpm db:migrate, db:migrate:dev),
#                                   which runs inside packages/db.
#
# Production: apps/web and apps/scheduler get their environment from the
# app host's service manager; judge hosts get /etc/recjudge/worker.env from
# infra/judge/cloud-init.yaml. compose.yaml needs no .env at all.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Prisma CLI: copy into packages/db/.env ───────────────────────────────
# Local Postgres 17 on port 5433 (scripts/dev/wsl-services.sh or compose.yaml).
# 127.0.0.1, not localhost: on Windows localhost resolves to ::1 first and
# WSL2 serves only the IPv4 loopback, so Prisma reports P1001 while the
# database is running (docs/RUNBOOK.md §1.8).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://recx:recx-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5433/recx"
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT="postgresql://recx:recx-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5433/recx"

# ── Scheduler: security email (apps/scheduler/.env.local or its service env) ──
# The EmailOutbox drain (docs/RUNBOOK.md §2.11). smtp | log | disabled.
# Default: log in development (subject and body to the scheduler log, never
# the address) and disabled elsewhere; log is refused in production.
# MAIL_TRANSPORT=log
# Required for smtp: smtp:// or smtps:// with credentials. Never logged.
# SMTP_URL="smtps://user:password@mail.example.invalid:465"
# MAIL_FROM="REC Code <no-reply@rec-code.invalid>"

# ── Opt-in test suites (set in the shell, not in a file) ─────────────────
#   RECX_DB_TESTS=1                 database-backed tests against recx_test
#   RECX_TEST_DATABASE_URL=...      default postgresql://recx:recx-dev-only@127.0.0.1:5433/recx_test
#                                   (always the IPv4 loopback, never localhost)
#   RECX_REDIS_TESTS=1              Redis-backed tests (REDIS_URL, default redis://127.0.0.1:6379)
#   RECX_ISOLATE_INTEGRATION=1      Linux sandbox integration tests (isolate + toolchains)
